From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:11:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: quiesce CPU workers and retire cached pools before
 process exit

The v11 CRT joins all pthreads, so static private Rayon pools cannot rely on process teardown. Retain AROS pool ownership explicitly and prevent recreation after shutdown. Track detached CPU producers, cancel application activity, wake paused face workers, wait for producer completion and only then terminate global Rayon. Preserve the upstream pool lifetime on other platforms.

Normalize all supported CLI file arguments, including MCP and merge inputs/preview output. Preserve optional connect parsing. Disable MCP stdio and network model/data downloads explicitly on AROS until cancellable stdin/DNS shutdown can be validated; no blocking helper is launched for these unsupported operations.

Verification: owned-pool, worker tracking, shared rendering parser, path conversion and CLI path regression tests pass on host (13 tests total); CPU dependency graph excludes GPU backends. Native final archive acceptance pending. No model, GPU or full upstream CI claim.
